    "narrative": "Today's lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers around high-efficiency volume, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (85.94) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98). **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Lowder and a favorable 4% bump for stolen base potential due to the pitcher's slow delivery. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** finds himself in an ideal spot; his score is significantly boosted by a combination of a hitter-friendly park, favorable wind, and a strong platoon advantage, making him a must-start despite the minor risk posed by the opposing catcher's pop time. **Gabriel Moreno** (70.08) rounds out our top tier, as his slot in the #3 hole combined with a weak 4.72 xERA opposing arm provides a high-floor, high-upside anchor for our production today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Cole Young** (44.13), who fell just shy of our rotation due to an unfavorable #8 lineup position and a sub-optimal matchup against Peterson. While we prioritize speed, the optimizer ultimately favored the efficiency of **Zach McKinstry** and **Max Muncy** to fill our middle infield and utility gaps, as their projected run-production metrics outweighed the marginal gains **Cole Young** might offer on the basepaths against a difficult lefty. Owners should monitor the 45% rain risk impacting **Travis Bazzana** and **Mickey Moniak**; while their underlying metrics are strong, any game delays could cap our daily production, and we have **Jose Caballero** and **Austin Riley** waiting in the wings should lineups shift or weather force late-inning tactical adjustments. We are also monitoring the health of **James Wood**, who remains on the IL, as his absence continues to consolidate our available OF scoring potential into the current core of **Griffin Conine**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Zach McKinstry**.",
